bind-entity-public-only: the bind check of an HMAC session skips public-only objects

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, "Authorization Checks"): "Authorization
checks must be performed in this order. 1. The public and sensitive portions
of the object shall be present on the TPM (`TPM_RC_AUTH_UNAVAILABLE`)."

For an HMAC session that is bound, CheckAuthSession() first decides whether
the authorized entity is the bind entity (IsSessionBindEntity() ->
SessionComputeBoundEntity()), which reads the entity's authValue with
EntityGetAuthValue(). For a public-only object that function asserts that the
sensitive area is loaded, so the TPM enters failure mode instead of reaching
the TPM_RC_AUTH_UNAVAILABLE check (IsAuthValueAvailable()). A public-only
object cannot be the bind entity (binding needs its authValue), so the patch
returns FALSE for it; the command then fails with TPM_RC_AUTH_UNAVAILABLE, as
in tpm-rs. Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
@@ -175,6 +175,16 @@
     if(session->attributes.isBound)
     {
         // Compute the bind value for the entity.
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+        // a public-only object has no authValue (EntityGetAuthValue() asserts), so it
+        // cannot be the bind entity.
+        if(HandleGetType(associatedHandle) == TPM_HT_TRANSIENT)
+        {
+            OBJECT* object = HandleToObject(associatedHandle);
+            if(object != NULL && !ObjectIsSequence(object)
+               && object->attributes.publicOnly == SET)
+                return FALSE;
+        }
         SessionComputeBoundEntity(associatedHandle, &entity);
 
         // Compare to the bind value in the session.
